sers/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-24T16:33:55Z","updated_at":"2015-12-09T10:16:00Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Claudiu Popa (BitBucket: [PCManticore](http://bitbucket.org/PCManticore), GitHub: @PCManticore)**:\n\n---\n\nOn how many files did you tested? I presume two, since two pylint processes appeared briefly. Initially, --jobs was added because some huge codebases at Intel were tested, if I'm not mistaken, and they had hundreds of files, leading to a huge amount of time spent in analyzing them with Pylint.  Another problem with --jobs is that we had to instantiate a new PyLinter class in each process, because otherwise there's no way to make it work on Windows and this brings additional time spent here as well. It would be great if we can find some ideas to improve the performance of --jobs.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163177009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163177011","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/467#issuecomment-163177011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/467","id":163177011,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE2MzE3NzAxMQ==","user":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-02-24T21:55:07Z","updated_at":"2015-12-09T10:16:00Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Pavel Roskin (BitBucket: [pavel_roskin](http://bitbucket.org/pavel_roskin))**:\n\n---\n\nWhen I made my measurements, I ran pylint on Frescobaldi source (https://github.com/wbsoft/frescobaldi) like this:\n\n```\npylint --jobs=11 frescobaldi_app\n```\n\nAlmost all python sources are under frescobaldi_app. I assumed operating on whole packages would be the best way to run pylint.\n\nBut then I tried\n\n```\nfind frescobaldi_app -name '*.py' | xargs pylint --jobs=11\n```\n\nThat worked much better and showed a good CPU load (close to 100%) and top was showing 11 processes. In that case removing `--jobs=11` increased the real time from 14 to 43 seconds (that's without `--py3k`).\n\nSo, it turns out to be a \"user error\". I would prefer not to use `find`, but that's a completely separate issue.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163177011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163177015","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/467#issuecomment-16317